{title: Full Assurance of Faith}
{subtitle: Hebrews 10:22–23}
{key: D}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | [G] | [D] | [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
We have [D]confidence to enter now
By the [Bm]blood of Jesus it allows
The [G]new and living way is clear
[A]Opened through the curtain
Through his [D]flesh the path is true
We [Bm]walk upon the ground so new
A [G]great priest stands over the [A]house
We [G]find our rest in his [D]grace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Draw near with a true heart today
In [Bm]the full assurance of faith
Our [G]hearts are sprinkled clean
From [A]the evil conscience pain
[G]Bodies washed with [A]pure water
[G]We [A]stand before the Fa[D]ther [G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Hold un[D]waveringly to the hope
[Bm]He who promised is faithful
Let us [G]spur one another on
[A]Toward love and good works
Not ne[D]glecting to meet together
As [Bm]some have made a habit
En[G]couraging one another more
As we [A]see the Day drawing [D]near
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Draw near with a true heart today
In the [Bm]full assurance of faith
Our [G]hearts are sprinkled clean
From [A]the evil conscience pain
[G]Bodies washed with [A]pure water
[G]We [A]stand before the Fa[D]ther
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dmaj7/C#]If we [Bm]deliberately go on sinning
[F#m]After receiving the knowledge
No [G]sacrifice for sins is left
[A]We must guard our hearts so well
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Draw [D]near with a true heart today
In the [Bm]full assurance of faith
Our [G]hearts are sprinkled clean
From [A]the evil conscience pain
[G]Bodies washed with [A]pure water
[G]We [A]stand before the Fa[D]ther
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[G]He who promised is [A]faithful
[G]We draw near [A]with a true heart
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
